  "result": {
    "engine": "jupyter",
    "markdown": "---\ngd-head-tags:\n  - >-\n    `<script type=\"application/ld+json\">[{\"@context\": \"https://schema.org\",\n    \"@type\": \"SoftwareSourceCode\", \"name\": \"EdgeCase\", \"description\":\n    \"High-performance graph analysis library\", \"codeRepository\":\n    \"https://github.com/rich-iannone/edgecase\", \"license\":\n    \"https://opensource.org/licenses/MIT\", \"url\":\n    \"https://rich-iannone.github.io/edgecase\", \"documentation\":\n    \"https://rich-iannone.github.io/edgecase\", \"programmingLanguage\": {\"@type\":\n    \"ComputerLanguage\", \"name\": \"Python\"}}, {\"@context\": \"https://schema.org\",\n    \"@type\": \"WebPage\", \"name\": \"Graph.mean_distance - EdgeCase\", \"isPartOf\":\n    {\"@type\": \"WebSite\", \"name\": \"EdgeCase\"}, \"url\":\n    \"https://rich-iannone.github.io/edgecase/reference/Graph.mean_distance.html\"}]</script>`{=html}\nopen-graph:\n  title: >-\n    [Graph.mean_distance()]{.doc-object-name .doc-function .doc-label\n    .doc-label-method} | EdgeCase\n  description: Get mean distance (average shortest path length).\ntwitter-card:\n  title: >-\n    [Graph.mean_distance()]{.doc-object-name .doc-function .doc-label\n    .doc-label-method} | EdgeCase\n  description: Get mean distance (average shortest path length).\ntitle: >-\n  [Graph.mean_distance()]{.doc-object-name .doc-function .doc-label\n  .doc-label-method}\nbody-classes: doc-api-page doc-py-api-page\nshift-heading-level-by: 0\nbread-crumbs: false\ntoc-depth: 3\ndescription-meta: Get mean distance (average shortest path length).\npage-navigation: false\nhtml-table-processing: none\n---\n\n::: {.doc-subject}\n\nGet mean distance (average shortest path length).\n:::\n\n::: {.doc-usage-source}\nUsage\n\n[Source](https://github.com/rich-iannone/edgecase/blob/main/python/edgecase/graph.py#L57687-L57793){target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"}\n:::\n\n::: {.doc-signature .doc-function}\n```pythonsignature\nGraph.mean_distance(unconnected=True)\n```\n:::\n\n::: {.doc-text}\n\n![Mean distance](../assets/graphs/mean-distance.light.svg){.lightbox fig-alt=\"A six-node graph and a card that adds the shortest-path distances of all 15 node pairs to 28 and divides by the 15 pairs, giving a mean distance of 1.867.\" width=\"100%\"}\n\nComputes average shortest path length between all reachable node pairs. Also known as\naverage path length or characteristic path length.\n\nDistances are counted in hops (number of edges) with a breadth-first search from every\nnode, so edge weights are ignored. In a directed graph a pair `(u, v)` counts only if `v`\ncan be reached from `u` by following edge directions, and `(u, v)` and `(v, u)` are\nseparate pairs. The cost is one traversal per node, roughly `O(n * (n + m))`.\n\nThe mean distance is a single-number summary of how compact a network is, and is used\nfor:\n\n- testing for small-world structure (short average paths despite local clustering)\n- comparing how quickly information or contagion can travel in different networks\n- tracking how a network's reach changes as nodes or edges are removed or added\n:::\n\n## Parameters {.doc-parameters}\n\n::: {.doc-definition-items}\n<code>[unconnected]{.doc-parameter-name}[:]{.doc-parameter-annotation-sep} [bool]{.doc-parameter-annotation} [=]{.doc-parameter-default-sep .op} [[True]{.va}]{.doc-parameter-default}</code>\n\n:   Controls what happens when some pairs of nodes cannot reach each other. If `True`\n    (default), unreachable pairs are simply left out and the result is the average over\n    all reachable pairs, pooled across components. If `False`, the method returns `None`\n    unless every node can reach every other node (for directed graphs, this means the\n    graph must be strongly connected).\n:::\n\n## Returns {.doc-returns}\n\n::: {.doc-definition-items}\n<code> [float]{.doc-parameter-annotation}</code>\n\n:   Average shortest path length, or `None` if graph is disconnected (when\n    `unconnected=False`). Also `None` for an empty graph or one in which no node can\n    reach any other.\n:::\n\n## Technical Notes {.doc-technical-notes}\n\nThe mean distance $\\bar{d} = \\dfrac{1}{|R|} \\sum_{(u, v) \\in R} d(u, v)$ is averaged\nonly over pairs $R$ that are actually reachable, which matters for directed or\ndisconnected graphs. This quantity, also called the *characteristic path length*, is\nwhat Watts and Strogatz used to identify small-world structure: real networks tend\nto display much shorter $\\bar{d}$ than a regular lattice of the same size while\nclustering stays lattice-like. In scale-free graphs, $\\bar{d}$ grows only\nlogarithmically with $|V|$, and $\\bar{d}$ itself appears in epidemiological\nestimates of average time-to-infection along a contact network.\n\n## See Also {.doc-see-also}\n\n[](`~diameter`) \n\n:   The longest of the shortest-path distances.\n\n[](`~wiener_index`) \n\n:   The sum of the distances over all pairs.\n\n[](`~global_efficiency`) \n\n:   The mean of the inverse distances, finite for disconnected graphs.\n\n## Examples {.doc-examples}\n\nIn a four-node path the six pairs are at distances 1, 2, 3, 1, 2, and 1, so the mean\ndistance is `10 / 6`, about `1.67`:\n\n::: {#f28c9b0c .cell execution_count=1}\n``` {.python .cell-code}\nimport edgecase as ec\n\ngraph = ec.Graph.from_edges([(\"A\", \"B\"), (\"B\", \"C\"), (\"C\", \"D\")])\n\ngraph.mean_distance()\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display execution_count=1}\n```\n1.6666666666666665\n```\n:::\n:::\n\n\nAdding a shortcut from A to D turns the path into a cycle and brings the far ends\ntogether, lowering the mean distance to `8 / 6`, about `1.33`:\n\n::: {#8bb9cd86 .cell execution_count=2}\n``` {.python .cell-code}\ngraph.add_edge(\"A\", \"D\")\ngraph.mean_distance()\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display execution_count=2}\n```\n1.3333333333333333\n```\n:::\n:::\n\n\nFor a disconnected graph, the default averages over the pairs that can reach each other.\nHere the pairs within the chain A-B-C (distances 1, 2, 1) and the pair D-E (distance 1)\ngive `5 / 4 = 1.25`, while `unconnected=False` refuses to answer and returns `None`:\n\n::: {#11f9d6fd .cell execution_count=3}\n``` {.python .cell-code}\nsplit = ec.Graph.from_edges([(\"A\", \"B\"), (\"B\", \"C\"), (\"D\", \"E\")])\n\nsplit.mean_distance(), split.mean_distance(unconnected=False)\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display execution_count=3}\n```\n(1.25, None)\n```\n:::\n:::\n\n\n### The average trip on the metro\n\n`metro()` is a made-up city's metro network. Over all 190 pairs of stations, a trip takes\n3.26 stops on average. An express from Central to the Airport (highlighted) brings the\naverage down to 3.05, and the longest trip from seven stops to six:\n\n::: {#5fa040e0 .cell execution_count=4}\n``` {.python .cell-code}\nmetro = ec.metro()\ntoday = metro.mean_distance()\n\nmetro.add_edge(\"Central\", \"Airport\", weight=12.0, line=\"Express\")\nround(today, 2), round(metro.mean_distance(), 2)\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display execution_count=4}\n```\n(3.26, 3.05)\n```\n:::\n:::\n\n\n::: {#8b8cc332 .cell execution_count=5}\n``` {.python .cell-code}\nmetro.plot(\n    layout=\"pos\", highlight_edges=[(\"Central\", \"Airport\")],\n    label_by=\"label\",\n)\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display execution_count=5}\n```{=html}\n<div class=\"ec-theme\" style=\"display:contents\"><style class=\"ec-theme-vars\">:where(.ec-theme){--ect-3239c383:#fafafa;--ect-e5dfd507:#94a3b8;--ect-8a2de1d4:#374151;--ect-57425a7e:rgba(15,23,42,0.88);--ect-21ade003:#f1f5f9;--ect-61169ea5:#c2410c;--ect-63cc1385:#d4d4d8;--ect-879b7ebc:#949497;--ect-b9f8de6d:#872d08;--ect-f59ba8df:#a1a1aa}@media (prefers-color-scheme: dark){.ec-theme{--ect-3239c383:#0d1117;--ect-e5dfd507:#4b5563;--ect-8a2de1d4:#d1d5db;--ect-57425a7e:rgba(241,245,249,0.92);--ect-21ade003:#0f172a;--ect-61169ea5:#f97316;--ect-63cc1385:#3f3f46;--ect-879b7ebc:#2c2c31;--ect-b9f8de6d:#ae500f;--ect-f59ba8df:#71717a}}:is(html.quarto-light, 